Confirmed: the `[:120]` truncation happens on raw `base` (before whitespace collapse), so the truncation boundary counts newlines/tabs as characters. After collapse, the visible query is shorter than 120 chars of actual content when the first 120 chars contained whitespace runs. This is a real but minor semantic point (and both channels share it, so no drift). 

